WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.304
Read the axes first. Temperature increases rightward; pressure increases downward. Heating

00:00:05.304 --> 00:00:09.808
moves the rock right. Crossing the solidus starts partial melting.

00:00:10.642 --> 00:00:15.229
Now move upward: pressure decreases while temperature stays similar. That is

00:00:15.229 --> 00:00:19.400
decompression melting. Watch melt appear between grains that remain solid.

00:00:20.642 --> 00:00:24.439
Water lowers the solidus. The same rock can start melting without

00:00:24.439 --> 00:00:28.237
becoming hotter. Know how all three changes appear on this graph.
